WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:07.730
In the last video Aleksa used an old technique to shoot and edit a TikTok.

2
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.130
And instead of returning to the present, he went even further

3
00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.530
and in this video he'll try, with cameras from the last century,

4
00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.090
to make a new photograph for Instagram.

5
00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.810
Will he succeed? Can an old camera beat the new ones?

6
00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.170
Find out from the daily press or watch the video to the end.

7
00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:24.060
While I was rummaging through old stuff for the previous video,

8
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.800
I came across an interesting thing.

9
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.500
It's my grandfather's camera.

10
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.420
And this is my great-grandfather's camera.

11
00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.420
I won't drag it out, you already know what I'll be doing today,

12
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.240
but in brief: I'll try to find film, come up with and take a photograph,

13
00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.840
develop this film and get a picture for Instagram.

14
00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.620
But I don't know yet whether these cameras work,

15
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.480
or whether film can be developed at home,

16
00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.280
or even how much all this will cost.

17
00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:50.460
I'm doing this at my own expense, my goal is to have fun

18
00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:52.840
and show you the whole process of shooting on film.

19
00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.060
Stay to the end and don't forget to subscribe.

20
00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.900
It was very hard to find a store that sells film.

21
00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.860
But at the Fotokiosk store I found everything I needed.

22
00:01:00.940 --> 00:01:02.260
I wanted to buy color film.

23
00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.880
But nowhere on the internet did I find chemicals for developing color film.

24
00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.000
So I played it safe.

25
00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.140
I ordered the cheapest film, because I'm sure I'll mess something up.

26
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.940
It costs 1100 dinars, with delivery it's about fifteen hundred.

27
00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:14.880
We add to the cart and order.

28
00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:18.040
Now we wait for the film to arrive, and while it's on its way, we have two tasks.

29
00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:21.520
The first task is to come up with what photograph I even want to post.

30
00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:24.200
And the second is to learn to use this marvel.

31
00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:26.080
First I took on this second task.

32
00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.820
I need to learn to use an analog camera.

33
00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.580
And, as every time I learn something new, my best friend was YouTube.

34
00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.080
And here's what I learned.

35
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.700
When we press the shutter of an analog camera,

36
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.700
an opening called the aperture opens.

37
00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:39.960
And it lets light through.

38
00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.020
This light passes through the lens, consisting of a series of glass elements,

39
00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.800
and then falls on the film that's inside the camera.

40
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:49.780
Film is actually a thin flexible strip made up of several layers.

41
00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.080
The main part of the film is the emulsion, the light-sensitive layer.

42
00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.780
That means it's sensitive to light.

43
00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:59.060
The emulsion consists of microscopic silver halides.

44
00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.160
When light hits the emulsion, it creates a latent image.

45
00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:04.060
The latent image is actually invisible,

46
00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.480
but it contains information about the intensity of light on certain parts of the scene.

47
00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.620
After the light is captured on the emulsion, the film has to be developed.

48
00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.460
The developing process consists of several chemical stages.

49
00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:17.560
First the film is immersed in developer, which turns the latent image into a visible one,

50
00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:20.280
and then it's placed in fixer so it keeps that appearance.

51
00:02:20.480 --> 00:02:23.700
The most important thing — until you develop the film,

52
00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.720
it must be in complete darkness.

53
00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:27.800
Either in the canister or in the camera.

54
00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:30.380
If while shooting the camera accidentally opens,

55
00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:31.930
all the photographs will be destroyed.

56
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:34.920
Yes, now it's much easier for me and not scary at all.

57
00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:38.440
Look what arrived.

58
00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:46.830
So, all I know — I mustn't unwind this strip,

59
00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:51.070
and when I insert it into the camera, I can't take it out until I've shot it all.

60
00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.290
And then I have to rewind it like this,

61
00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:56.890
and only then can I take out and develop the film.

62
00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.570
Do not enter, developing film.

63
00:02:59.950 --> 00:03:02.810
In any case I wouldn't trust myself much in all this,

64
00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.290
so I'll still study and look around a bit more.

65
00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.890
I have a huge problem, folks.

66
00:03:07.310 --> 00:03:11.670
Two days have passed, and I'm still scared to put this film in the camera.

67
00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:14.690
I don't know why, I'm scared I'll mess something up,

68
00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.710
scared the whole film will go to waste.

69
00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:21.590
I've been reading and studying these cameras, this film for several days,

70
00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:24.550
and the worst thing that can happen is that the whole film is lost.

71
00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.350
The question: am I really that unlucky?

72
00:03:26.710 --> 00:03:28.310
Maybe so, it's possible,

73
00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:30.010
but I decided it's worth it

74
00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:31.910
and that it's okay even if the whole film is ruined.

75
00:03:32.070 --> 00:03:33.450
I'll buy a new one, shoot this video.

76
00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:34.910
It's only fifteen hundred dinars.

77
00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.610
Are you ready for me to insert this?

78
00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:40.310
So, the first thing to do is open the camera, of course.

79
00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.910
We lower this down and lift the cover.

80
00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:46.130
We take the film and this part that goes up,

81
00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:50.070
into here, goes in, so, here.

82
00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:54.410
What rotates on top, we take like this and lift.

83
00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:56.590
So, now the film can go inside.

84
00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:58.950
Come on, and that's it.

85
00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.110
And now the part I'm afraid of,

86
00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:04.490
because often this thing doesn't grip the film well.

87
00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:08.010
And I'm hoping now that everything's as it should be, it seems.

88
00:04:08.490 --> 00:04:09.730
Oh yes, it holds, oh, great.

89
00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:17.490
All right, I'll open it to see whether at least a little has wound on.

90
00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:18.710
No!

91
00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:19.490
Oh.

92
00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.250
Grab it, please, please.

93
00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:24.790
It should pass here, and then come out here.

94
00:04:26.650 --> 00:04:27.170
Got it!

95
00:04:27.790 --> 00:04:29.710
It worked, it worked!

96
00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.590
That's another matter, let's go.

97
00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:37.230
It wasn't visible on the camera, but I managed to hook it.

98
00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:38.450
Well, that's it, it's ready.

99
00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:42.230
We've loaded the film, and now I need to take the first test shot.

100
00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:43.990
When it's cloudy, that is, a bit dark,

101
00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:48.070
we shoot at a shutter speed of 60, aperture 5.6.

102
00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:52.860
So, I just clicked the last frame,

103
00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:54.600
and if this turns, it means all is well.

104
00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:56.500
It doesn't turn.

105
00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:57.260
What the fuck?

106
00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:59.760
If while shooting the camera accidentally opens,

107
00:05:00.040 --> 00:05:01.980
all the photographs will be destroyed.

108
00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:03.740
No, now I've exposed it all.

109
00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.920
I exposed all the shots I took.

110
00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:07.320
The right thing to say is "photograph," not "shot."

111
00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:11.230
Oh, now it turns!

112
00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:12.630
I exposed four shots.

113
00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:14.150
Now let me shoot properly.

114
00:05:16.870 --> 00:05:18.630
Now we move on to the second task —

115
00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:20.730
coming up with what the photo will look like.

116
00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:23.050
Here, like this, there will be some car.

117
00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:25.290
Only now do I realize how stupid this idea is.

118
00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:26.390
This is my head.

119
00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:28.950
This leg is, like, stretched out like this.

120
00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:31.490
This is my arm.

121
00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:32.930
Erase all this.

122
00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:35.950
I could take a photo in the library.

123
00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.670
These photographs look somehow familiar.

124
00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:39.980
Oh yes!

125
00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:41.700
Oh, I like this!

126
00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:42.660
I like this!

127
00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:45.300
And I know exactly where I could be photographed like this.

128
00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:46.580
But I don't have such hair.

129
00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:50.020
We have a photo, folks, here, I'll show you, from this angle.

130
00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.460
Something like this is what I want.

131
00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.880
Maybe a slightly different angle.

132
00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:54.840
The background will be a bit different.

133
00:05:55.080 --> 00:05:56.800
But I want to make exactly this kind of shot.

134
00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:01.540
I packed everything inside.

135
00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:03.080
And here we are, this is the day when

136
00:06:03.560 --> 00:06:04.960
we actually take these photos.

137
00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:06.700
Now I'll first take a few test shots.

138
00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:07.500
Here's Anđela.

139
00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:08.600
Wave to the people.

140
00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:09.700
Look what we have.

141
00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.520
No idea what settings to use.

142
00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:12.440
I'm doing everything blind.

143
00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:14.160
It's my first time shooting on film.

144
00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:15.800
So let's see what comes out.

145
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:21.500
And one more thing.

146
00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:26.700
Now I'll explain to Anđela

147
00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:28.560
how to use this camera.

148
00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:29.980
Now she'll try to photograph me.

149
00:06:30.620 --> 00:06:31.160
So.

150
00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:50.260
Like a portrait.

151
00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.170
First she shoots me with a phone,

152
00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:54.970
so I can see

153
00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.410
whether I like the frame or not.

154
00:06:56.530 --> 00:06:57.850
I can shoot only once.

155
00:06:57.970 --> 00:06:58.530
Literally — and that's it.

156
00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:03.350
That's it.

157
00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:03.650
Bravo.

158
00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:04.570
It worked.

159
00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:05.510
This kind of shot

160
00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.310
is what I want her to take with this film camera.

161
00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:09.130
Sure.

162
00:07:09.230 --> 00:07:09.990
Are you ready?

163
00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:10.870
Let's go.

164
00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:26.960
Folks, that's it.

165
00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:29.980
My Instagram photo is right here now, inside.

166
00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:33.240
And we'll see it in about a week,

167
00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:34.700
when the film comes to me.

168
00:07:35.140 --> 00:07:36.540
And it seems to me it turned out well.

169
00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:37.600
I'll go shoot a bit more,

170
00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:39.280
and then we'll look at the results.

171
00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:40.820
So, you see this on top.

172
00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:41.960
You unfold it.

173
00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:43.000
It looks like this.

174
00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:45.660
You just press this one from below on the other side

175
00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:47.980
and wind in this direction.

176
00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:50.500
When you feel there's no resistance anymore,

177
00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.480
you open the camera,

178
00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.060
lift this up.

179
00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:54.500
Hop.

180
00:07:56.180 --> 00:07:57.620
The film falls out by itself.

181
00:07:57.920 --> 00:07:58.820
The film is shot.

182
00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:01.020
I hope most of the shots turned out well.

183
00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:03.360
But the main thing for me is that the one for Instagram turns out.

184
00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:04.860
Because that's the point of this video.

185
00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:07.360
Now this film has to go off for developing.

186
00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:11.080
I had a huge desire to develop the film at home myself.

187
00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:14.340
So I searched online for how much all the equipment would cost me.

188
00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:15.540
And listen to this.

189
00:08:15.880 --> 00:08:19.280
All together it would come to roughly seven and a half thousand dinars.

190
00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:21.840
I have absolutely no intention of paying that kind of money

191
00:08:21.840 --> 00:08:24.960
to develop shots that may not have turned out.

192
00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:26.580
But instead I found this.

193
00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:30.680
The same company where I bought the film also has a developing service.

194
00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.180
And it costs 690 dinars.

195
00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:35.780
I wanted to do everything myself, go through the whole process myself,

196
00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:38.840
but it's impossible and too expensive.

197
00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:42.020
Someday, when I can afford such investments in a single video,

198
00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:44.460
I will, of course, invest, but for now it's pointless.

199
00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:46.160
Well, let's see what happens.

200
00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:51.440
Here, I packed the film in here — who even sends anything by mail now?

201
00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:59.970
In fact the film hasn't arrived yet, I had to do the animation this way.

202
00:09:00.070 --> 00:09:01.790
But they sent me the shots.

203
00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:02.570
They scanned them.

204
00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:06.090
For the first time, premiere: we're looking at the shots with you.

205
00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:07.530
The first shot — my setup.

206
00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:09.110
The next shot — my room.

207
00:09:09.270 --> 00:09:11.490
It's blurry, and that, honestly, worries me.

208
00:09:11.670 --> 00:09:13.430
Because if I didn't get focus here,

209
00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:15.450
most likely I didn't get focus anywhere.

210
00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:18.270
Here I shot myself, it's a selfie.

211
00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:19.150
A black-and-white selfie.

212
00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:20.390
It's actually not that bad.

213
00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:25.700
It's a very beautiful shot.

214
00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:27.260
It's a gorgeous shot.

215
00:09:27.560 --> 00:09:28.360
Wow, wow.

216
00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.160
And then she shot me.

217
00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:33.960
And then she shot me like this.

218
00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:39.620
Ooh, this is actually the best shot.

219
00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:44.180
This is actually the best shot I've taken with a camera.

220
00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:45.000
Wow.

221
00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:46.840
It's a good shot.

222
00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:49.000
Next we have David.

223
00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:50.160
That's also a very good shot.

224
00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:51.520
This is Anđela and David.

225
00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:00.640
You know what?

226
00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:01.780
Actually I have an idea.

227
00:10:02.020 --> 00:10:03.540
I actually have a very good idea.

228
00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.340
in Photoshop, to make this shot sharper.

229
00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:09.560
Good idea.

230
00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:13.940
Remember, at the start of the video I said I wouldn't post black-and-white shots?

231
00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:15.900
Because color film is more expensive,

232
00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:18.920
and the developing process is much more complicated, hence more expensive too.

233
00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:23.080
So I took black-and-white shots, and now we'll colorize them.

234
00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.400
Although the same can be done in Photoshop,

235
00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.900
this artificial intelligence is much better.

236
00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.400
The site is called Palette.fm.

237
00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.740
All you need is to take your photograph,

238
00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:35.680
drag it onto the site

239
00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:38.260
and wait for the AI to do its work.

240
00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:40.220
This is like the basic color palette,

241
00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:43.560
and wait, I'll upload all the possible options, and we'll see what comes out.

242
00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:45.540
This is the basic one, and, as far as I can see,

243
00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:48.080
it actually did a pretty good job.

244
00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:49.100
Looks wonderful.

245
00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:50.280
And what do we do now?

246
00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:53.220
You have the option to download for free and in HD,

247
00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.200
but you have to pay for that.

248
00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.940
That is, you simply download this free version,

249
00:10:56.940 --> 00:10:58.200
and once downloaded,

250
00:10:58.780 --> 00:11:03.100
you just overlay it in Photoshop on top of the original shot.

251
00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:05.300
Set a filter, color — and that's it.

252
00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:08.140
You have full quality, and you haven't paid anything.

253
00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:10.360
We Balkan people really love free things.

254
00:11:10.560 --> 00:11:14.100
No, well look, every shot you took on film

255
00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:15.960
actually has an awesome vibe.

256
00:11:16.260 --> 00:11:19.100
Don't forget to hit that red "subscribe" button,

257
00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:23.080
because the next video will be in a completely different format,

258
00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:25.240
it will be a bit creepy, it's about a horror theme,

259
00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:26.900
but examined from a scientific point of view,

